WEBVTT

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:12.490
Oh! It's starting everyone!

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:32.050
It's so pretty!

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:35.380
Coming to see the fireworks
has really paid off huh?

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:39.970
It’s really amazing to see fireworks
and Mt. Fuji at the same time!

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:41.140
Really.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:44.640
Sensei!
The fireworks have started!

00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:53.650
It’s about ready isn’t it?

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.610
And up we go…

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:00.160
Wow!

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:01.910
The chicken’s all done!

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:04.660
We’re all set over here too!

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.670
Thanks for the food!

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:23.680
Delicious!

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:26.140
Wow, it’s really good with the sour sauce!

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:28.980
And the chicken’s Cooked to perfection
isn’t it?

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:31.440
Delicious!

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:43.950
There there, it’s alright.

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:54.960
You have to choose between eating and talking, you know.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:03:00.260
If you don’t focus on chewing you’ll choke on it!

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.740
Camping when we’re all adults, huh?

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:31.250
Well, it’s certainly true we’ll all
probably have more money then.

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:34.750
There will be more we can do.
Maybe even how we camp will change!

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:37.840
Well I for one want a wood-burning
oven by then.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.260
With that, we could camp any time
of the year, couldn’t we?

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:43.680
In that case Chikuwa could probably
come camping with us!

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:51.270
When I get my license,
I want to go camping all over.

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:54.940
I’ll get all sorts of local ingredients
and make amazing food.

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:56.770
That would be nice.

00:03:56.860 --> 00:03:58.780
What about you, Rin?

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:04.660
I think… it would be cool to
get a bigger bike and go camping abroad.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.330
Wow…

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:07.910
That would be amazing

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:16.420
I want us all to camp together,
even when we’re older…

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:22.630
Agreed…

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:51.240
Shachihoko Publishing

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:08.470
Editorial

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:53.660
Let's get to it.

00:06:58.540 --> 00:06:59.830
Mornin’.

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:02.080
Good morning.

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:06.170
Mr. Kariya, didn’t you just get back
from traveling?

00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:11.140
Be that as it may, I have an article that
needs to be written before noon.

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:16.430
Ugh, our editor is just
a real piece of work.

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:19.600
Speaking of early isn’t this early for you
Ms. Shima?

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:23.770
I guess I just haven’t adjusted
to being in a new department.

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:25.320
Oh yeah…

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:27.440
Here’s a souvenir for you!

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:31.240
Yamanashi style Tsukapon…

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:33.570
Oh are you from there?

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:36.200
I am. Thank a lot.

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:40.000
Huh? You're still working on this?

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:39.310
Cute and trendy!

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:39.310
A tour of Nagoya's Cafe's
Project Proposal

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:42.750
I thought you had already submitted this.

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:46.500
It didn’t really turn out well…
This time though, it will work.

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:00.140
For this feature…

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:03.520
I'd like to cover trendy cafes in Nagoya
that are popular with young women.

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:06.900
Featuring Ogura-style toast and
other in-fashion sweets.

00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:12.030
The idea is to introduce the trendy and fashionable
charms of Nagoya.

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:17.870
The feature will focus on such places that you
can enjoy in the Meieki Sakae area.

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:20.040
We want to make these cafes destination travel.

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:27.860
REJECTED

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:40.680
I’m headed out for lunch to
check out new releases at the bookstore.

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:45.060
Ah, I’ll have the proof mocked up by 2.
See you then.

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:46.310
Will do.

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:13.530
I can see Fuji!

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:26.230
Oh!

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:28.790
Even from Tokyo it’s really visible.

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:27.120
There we go!

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:37.970
All done, Ms. Kagamihara?

00:10:38.050 --> 00:10:39.180
It’s perfect!

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:43.970
Yeah…
It really has a nice feel, huh?

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:52.310
By the way, isn’t tomorrow your day off?
Going to the mountains again?

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:55.150
I was actually thinking of
going to see my parents.

00:10:55.570 --> 00:10:57.900
My sister’s going to be home for
the first time in a long time.

00:10:57.990 --> 00:10:59.450
Uh…
Hello there.

00:11:00.070 --> 00:11:01.450
Welcome in!

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:04.450
We’re looking for a portable
fire pit?(??)

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:08.460
We thought we’d give
off-season camping a try.

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:10.210
That sounds nice!

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:12.830
Winter and Fall camping are
also really fun!

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:14.800
This one is

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:18.970
our all purpose model that
can also be used for cooking.

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:21.260
Using it to cook would definitely be nice…

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:25.970
Though it sure costs a bit huh?

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:28.980
Can we really do that much camping
in cold weather?

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:31.480
She's still pretty young.

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:34.230
Hmm… well you have a point…

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:37.440
Ah, so during the summer

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:39.900
You all go camping together, right?

00:11:39.990 --> 00:11:41.240
Correct.

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:45.200
If that’s the case,
then cooking over a fire
wouldn’t really be practical

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:47.240
How about a more standard model instead?

00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:51.160
If that’s okay then we have something
that is much cheaper.

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:52.830
That sounds good!

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:56.500
It does!
And that model would be…

00:11:56.920 --> 00:12:02.180
Oh, we don’t have it here,
but you can find it at the place
across the street!

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:05.010
Thank you for coming in!

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:07.510
Byebye!

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:09.520
Bye bye!

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:13.150
You know, you can also sell our stuff.

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:16.400
Eehehe. Sorry boss.

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:22.360
Well, I don’t think that today
will be the last time they’ll stop by.

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:23.490
Heh.

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:26.280
Ah! Here it is!

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:29.200
The one on display over there.

00:12:30.450 --> 00:12:34.040
Huh?? A gas… lantern?

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:37.000
It’s a bit costly, huh?

00:12:37.090 --> 00:12:38.750
But isn’t it so small and cute?

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:41.720
Wait… do you even go camping?

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:44.800
U-uh… well…

00:12:45.390 --> 00:12:47.350
Would you like to see it lit?

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:48.970
Huh?

00:13:06.910 --> 00:13:08.410
So pretty…

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.540
It’s so cool!
There’s something calming about it.

00:13:45.150 --> 00:13:47.320
My first weekend off in so long…

00:13:49.450 --> 00:13:51.370
It’s the best.

00:13:56.160 --> 00:14:00.750
Last month was Mie…
Let’s go somewhere further in this time.

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:09.030
Incoming Message

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:17.960
Hey! I’m in your area today!

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:21.900
Huh？

00:14:40.170 --> 00:14:44.000
Phew! It’s been too long, hasn’t it?

00:14:44.090 --> 00:14:46.630
When was the last time we saw eachother?

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:49.470
As I said, at the camping trip 3 years ago…

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:51.720
Were you even listening to me?

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:55.680
Nagoya’s chicken wings
are truly the best, aren’t they?!

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:59.310
You’re really a pain when you’re drunk, Chiaki.

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:02.940
Sorry but could I get another beer?

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:12.070
With all our varying schedules
I don’t often see anyone from then.

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:14.870
Oh yeah, Nadeshiko recently
sent me a message.

00:15:14.950 --> 00:15:15.950
Yep.

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:25.670
She’s looking as energetic as ever.

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:27.460
Here’s your beer!

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:31.300
So… Gone camping lately?

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:34.760
Well, since I’ve transferred out here
it’s been tough to get out.

00:15:34.850 --> 00:15:37.180
Oh yeah, to editorial right?
How’s it going?

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:39.230
Well, it’s going…

00:15:39.310 --> 00:15:41.560
How are things with you?

00:15:41.650 --> 00:15:45.320
How am I? How am I, huh…?

00:15:51.530 --> 00:15:53.030
- I quit!
- Huh!?

00:15:53.110 --> 00:15:57.370
I mean, I quit long ago and
went back to Yamanashi…

00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:58.830
So you returned?

00:15:58.910 --> 00:16:03.540
Nice to meet you! I’m Ogaki from the
Yamanashi Tourism Promotion Organization.

00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:07.500
Tourism… promotion?
What even is that?

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:10.260
Regardless what it means,
we’ll make Yamanashi lively!

00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:13.840
What in the world are you?

00:16:13.930 --> 00:16:17.640
I was dressed up as a dogū sculpture
for a product expo!

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:21.980
The main thing I’m working on now is a
revitalization plan for the Takaori area.

00:16:22.060 --> 00:16:23.480
Takaori？

00:16:23.560 --> 00:16:26.440
A nearby facility went belly up
a few years ago

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:28.690
and left behind a pretty big plot of land.

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:32.570
It’s be a shame to leave it empty,
so I was told to figure something out.

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:35.120
Even though it's a nice opportunity

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:36.950
what would we do
with all that space?

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:43.330
If it’s so big, wouldn’t a campsite
be a good idea?

00:16:43.420 --> 00:16:44.580
Woah…

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:54.050
Bill please!

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:55.640
Seargant Shima!

00:16:55.720 --> 00:16:59.310
Tell me a bit more about this
genius idea of yours!

00:16:59.390 --> 00:17:00.560
Huh?!

00:17:03.390 --> 00:17:05.230
Take us to Fujikawa in Yamanashi please!
And step on it!

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:07.310
- Hey wait！
- You‘ve got it miss！

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:12.690
Wh-where are you taking me?!?

00:17:13.110 --> 00:17:16.070
Let’s go to Takaori!

00:17:29.460 --> 00:17:33.130
Takeshita district in Fujikawa
Yamanashi Prefecture

00:17:33.210 --> 00:17:35.300
Also known as the town of the rising sun

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:39.510
because the sun peeks out of the
top of Mt. Fuji at the end of December.

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:41.970
This “Diamond Fuji” is well known.

00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:43.810
Thank you for the business!

00:17:49.150 --> 00:17:51.230
We really came all the way here…

00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:54.530
Come on, what remains of the facility
is over there.

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:03.950
It sure is run down.

00:18:04.040 --> 00:18:06.500
Well it closed down 5 years ago.

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:08.330
If we wanted a campsite here,

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:11.630
even just cleaning up and making
it pretty would be tough.

00:18:11.710 --> 00:18:14.260
I wasn’t serious when I suggested a-

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:16.970
Hey…

00:18:24.350 --> 00:18:27.770
I can’t really call for a ride home
until morning, so I’ll wait.

00:18:35.070 --> 00:18:38.660
Phew… Nice and warm…

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:04.680
Spooky…

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:08.620
Fujikawa Youth Nature Center

00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:08.560
It really is totally abandoned, huh.

00:19:08.890 --> 00:19:13.110
Makes sense, given where it was built.

00:19:13.190 --> 00:19:15.320
It’s in a pretty tucked away location.

00:19:16.990 --> 00:19:20.320
Pretty big inside…
If we fixed it up it could be pretty nice…

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:22.820
there’s even toilets.

00:19:32.170 --> 00:19:36.170
Oh, it’s sortof like a staircase.

00:19:51.980 --> 00:19:53.520
Let’s… go this way.

00:20:02.780 --> 00:20:04.490
An area for water…

00:20:06.780 --> 00:20:08.410
but it’s not running.

00:20:09.660 --> 00:20:13.290
Hm? What could that be?

00:20:18.960 --> 00:20:22.630
A jungle gym? Probably not.

00:20:23.640 --> 00:20:25.600
Is there stuff even further down?

00:20:36.770 --> 00:20:38.650
A tool shed…

00:20:39.530 --> 00:20:44.240
It’s pretty tasteful,
I wonder if it was custom-made.

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:59.920
Is that it… huh?

00:22:21.380 --> 00:22:23.050
Take a look around?

00:22:29.760 --> 00:22:33.220
The grass is all patchy and what remains
of the facility is in ruins.

00:22:33.970 --> 00:22:37.190
Perfect for a camp ground, huh?

00:22:38.600 --> 00:22:39.980
As I said I don’t…

00:22:40.060 --> 00:22:41.270
The truth is

00:22:42.270 --> 00:22:46.440
I also felt this place could be
a great campsite.

00:22:46.530 --> 00:22:49.910
I had already talked to my boss
and gotten permission.

00:22:51.950 --> 00:22:53.280
So, well...

00:22:53.910 --> 00:22:57.540
I liked living in Kyoto, at least,
that’s what I told myself.

00:22:57.620 --> 00:22:59.920
But I was drawn to this job because

00:23:00.420 --> 00:23:03.800
It seemed so fun
when I first heard about it.

00:23:06.630 --> 00:23:10.050
I guess I just love this area.

00:23:11.840 --> 00:23:14.010
And when I was back in Kyoto,

00:23:14.100 --> 00:23:17.060
the loneliness started to creep in
bit by bit.

00:23:17.640 --> 00:23:20.690
As for this place, it used to be a place
for everyone to come.

00:23:20.770 --> 00:23:23.480
A place made so they could have fun,
right?

00:23:24.270 --> 00:23:28.320
A place like that sounds better than Kyoto, to me.

00:23:32.160 --> 00:23:34.280
We have no budget and little manpower,

00:23:34.370 --> 00:23:38.290
Bbut regardless I was going to go out and
recruit some volunteers to help.

00:23:38.790 --> 00:23:39.830
So that being said…

00:23:40.330 --> 00:23:43.080
Why don’t we try to make it? Together.

00:24:04.190 --> 00:24:05.400
I’ll consider it…

00:24:11.650 --> 00:24:13.320
There we go, Sergeant Shima!

00:24:13.410 --> 00:24:15.450
I’ll be believing in you!!

00:24:15.530 --> 00:24:17.620
He-hey wait…

00:24:17.700 --> 00:24:19.870
- Hey！
- Huh？

00:24:23.920 --> 00:24:27.380
Rin! Aki!

00:24:27.460 --> 00:24:30.210
- Eh?
- Na-Nadeshkio?

00:24:34.680 --> 00:24:36.510
It’s been so long!!

00:24:36.600 --> 00:24:39.770
What are you doing here Nadeshiko?

00:24:40.180 --> 00:24:44.190
What? Aki told me to meet you two here.

00:24:44.270 --> 00:24:45.270
Huh？

00:24:45.630 --> 00:24:48.040
Rin and chicken wings, a great pair!

00:24:48.960 --> 00:24:52.840
That meter sure is real high!!

00:24:48.960 --> 00:24:52.840
We’re en route to Yamanashi by Taxi!

00:24:53.630 --> 00:24:56.340
Let’s all meet at the top,
everyone!              .

00:24:57.870 --> 00:25:00.620
Don’t tell me you also sent these
to Aoi and Saito…

00:25:00.700 --> 00:25:02.290
Eheheh

00:25:02.370 --> 00:25:05.540
Wait? So this wasn’t a get-together?

00:25:05.630 --> 00:25:08.420
I’m so sorry you had to drive all the way
from Tokyo!

00:25:08.500 --> 00:25:09.840
Oh! No worries!

00:25:09.920 --> 00:25:12.760
I’ve been back since last night.

00:25:12.840 --> 00:25:14.050
That’s it！

00:25:14.550 --> 00:25:17.550
After this, do you guys want some hot pot？

00:25:18.100 --> 00:25:19.310
Huh?

00:25:28.940 --> 00:25:31.360
- Crab!
- Amazing!

00:25:31.440 --> 00:25:33.530
I brought it back as a gift for my sister~

00:25:34.150 --> 00:25:35.950
Please, eat up.

00:25:37.530 --> 00:25:39.620
There’s even plenty left for seconds.

00:25:39.700 --> 00:25:41.660
You’ve got it!

00:25:43.790 --> 00:25:46.210
Thank you for the food!

00:25:50.460 --> 00:25:51.840
So good!

00:25:55.420 --> 00:25:58.340
You can taste the crab
from the first bite. Amazing!

00:25:58.800 --> 00:26:02.520
I can feel the warmth of the broth
spreading throughout my frozen body…

00:26:03.180 --> 00:26:08.730
Full of fluffy tofu
and soup stock full of Napa cabbage.

00:26:09.110 --> 00:26:13.480
Not to mention the green onion
and shiitake mushrooms and finally…

00:26:24.950 --> 00:26:29.250
Heavenly Crab!

00:26:51.610 --> 00:26:54.400
Come on… ouch！

00:27:20.630 --> 00:27:22.550
OUCH!

00:27:46.620 --> 00:27:48.830
Y’all are so silent…

00:27:50.120 --> 00:27:51.960
Sorry for the delay.

00:27:52.040 --> 00:27:54.210
Inuko! When did you get here?

00:27:54.290 --> 00:27:56.590
Oh I just got here.

00:27:56.670 --> 00:28:00.590
Not that ya noticed,
what with the crabs and all.

00:28:04.510 --> 00:28:07.100
Wow, that was so good!

00:28:07.430 --> 00:28:11.560
- It’s been a long time since I’ve seen you two.
- Yeah.

00:28:11.640 --> 00:28:13.900
Weren’t you working today?

00:28:13.980 --> 00:28:17.020
The elementary school has been
real busy recently.

00:28:17.110 --> 00:28:19.360
But at least Saturday
is usually an off day.

00:28:19.440 --> 00:28:21.570
What about Ena? Can she come?

00:28:21.650 --> 00:28:24.870
She’s working open to close today.

00:28:24.930 --> 00:28:26.680
Sorry, today won’t work.

00:28:25.490 --> 00:28:29.750
I guess the weekend is a busy time for a pet salon, huh?

00:28:37.800 --> 00:28:41.130
… so to summarize,
I’m going to make a campsite.

00:28:41.630 --> 00:28:43.090
That’s a bit out of the blue.

00:28:43.180 --> 00:28:45.720
A camp? You’re making a campsite?

00:28:45.800 --> 00:28:47.510
Contain your excitement, Nadeshiko.

00:28:47.600 --> 00:28:50.430
As I asked earlier, are you really
going through with it?

00:28:50.520 --> 00:28:53.310
I am! Is everyone with me?

00:28:53.390 --> 00:28:56.110
Rin told me about how much she
wants to do it.

00:28:56.190 --> 00:28:58.020
I’m not really that-

00:28:58.110 --> 00:28:59.480
Let’s do it!

00:28:59.570 --> 00:29:03.320
It would be so fun to make a campsite
with everyone!

00:29:03.400 --> 00:29:05.660
But is this really alright?

00:29:05.740 --> 00:29:07.740
Aki and I live nearby…

00:29:07.830 --> 00:29:11.700
But Nadeshiko is in Tokyo,
Ena’s in Yokohama…

00:29:11.790 --> 00:29:14.170
And Rin is down in Nagoya.

00:29:14.540 --> 00:29:17.290
It’s okay! We’ll make it work somehow!

00:29:17.750 --> 00:29:19.300
Right, Rin?!

00:29:19.360 --> 00:29:21.940
Well.. uh…

00:29:21.940 --> 00:29:22.800
Yeah.

00:29:24.550 --> 00:29:27.930
You’re really as energetic as ever,
huh, Nadeshiko?

00:29:29.890 --> 00:29:31.220
Alright!

00:29:31.310 --> 00:29:34.060
Ena has also given the go-ahead!

00:29:34.140 --> 00:29:36.190
Everyone’s in, then!

00:29:36.270 --> 00:29:41.030
Starting today, all five of us are
going to work together
and makes a campsite!

00:29:41.110 --> 00:29:44.240
To reach that goal, I’m going to give
each of you your own role!

00:29:44.320 --> 00:29:45.320
Huh？

00:29:45.860 --> 00:29:48.740
First up, Nadeshiko is the foreman.

00:29:52.200 --> 00:29:54.330
Inuko will attend to the schedule.

00:29:57.290 --> 00:29:58.630
Ena will be our PR.

00:30:01.750 --> 00:30:04.590
I’ll be taking care of stuff
stuff behind the scenes.

00:30:07.260 --> 00:30:10.850
And finally, the leader of this
campsite project is…

00:30:11.850 --> 00:30:12.850
Rin!

00:30:12.930 --> 00:30:14.230
Geh!!

00:30:15.480 --> 00:30:20.230
With all her strength and energy
Nadeshiko is the perfect foreman!

00:30:20.310 --> 00:30:23.030
Leave the hard work to me!

00:30:23.110 --> 00:30:28.160
Dead on, right? I’ve been thinking
about what everyone would be best at.

00:30:28.240 --> 00:30:31.780
W-w-wait, a minute.
Why do I have to be leader?

00:30:31.870 --> 00:30:32.870
Hmm?

00:30:32.950 --> 00:30:36.080
Because you’ve been
camping all your life..

00:30:36.160 --> 00:30:37.500
You’re the right person, right？

00:30:37.580 --> 00:30:39.750
When I think of camping, I think of you, Rin!

00:30:43.130 --> 00:30:45.260
We’ll be in your care, leader!

00:30:45.340 --> 00:30:48.380
I’ll try my best to not be
too much of a burden.

00:30:59.460 --> 00:31:01.960
Nadeshiko’s driving me over.

00:31:02.210 --> 00:31:05.590
Okay. I’ll have to thank her.

00:31:12.450 --> 00:31:16.040
I really wonder if we can do this.

00:31:21.040 --> 00:31:26.420
But… isn’t there something sortof exciting
about starting something new?

00:31:58.220 --> 00:32:05.230
Next time, let’s plan.
out the campsite!

00:32:01.770 --> 00:32:05.270
The prefectural office requires
that we submit a plan.

00:32:05.360 --> 00:32:10.780
Hey there! I’ll go with
you next time.

00:32:10.900 --> 00:32:14.280
Yeah yeah!

00:32:12.030 --> 00:32:14.280
Long time no see, Ena

00:32:12.160 --> 00:32:16.530
Next time meet at the prefectural office.

00:32:14.410 --> 00:32:18.290
I’m counting on all of you!

00:32:16.660 --> 00:32:18.290
Roger!!

00:32:41.410 --> 00:32:44.120
Nadeshiko told me everything

00:32:44.460 --> 00:32:46.460
You’re going to build a campsite, right？

00:32:46.540 --> 00:32:48.300
- Yeah.
- Hehe.

00:32:48.380 --> 00:32:51.090
I heard you’re the leader.
Isn’t that cool?

00:32:51.170 --> 00:32:54.430
Ah… I wouldn’t say it’s cool exactly.

00:32:56.850 --> 00:33:00.390
How long does it take for you to get to
the campsite by bike?

00:33:00.470 --> 00:33:03.190
Hmm…
It’s about 4 hours from Nagoya.

00:33:03.270 --> 00:33:04.850
4 hours!?

00:33:04.940 --> 00:33:07.610
Doesn’t that make this a bit hard, then?

00:33:07.690 --> 00:33:09.650
Surprisingly, not really.

00:33:10.030 --> 00:33:13.240
My grandpa would ride that bike
all the way to Yamanashi and back.

00:33:13.570 --> 00:33:16.200
You’re as strong headed as him.

00:33:17.530 --> 00:33:21.120
Ms. Shima, your oil change is done.

00:33:21.200 --> 00:33:23.790
Ah, thanks a lot.

00:33:26.960 --> 00:33:29.040
Yeah, looks good.

00:33:29.130 --> 00:33:32.420
You’re looking good too, Rin.

00:33:34.220 --> 00:33:37.430
Is… is that so?

00:33:38.890 --> 00:33:42.430
From here on out, there’s a lot I need
to look into and do, but…

00:33:42.520 --> 00:33:46.350
If it means I get to be with my
hometown friends,I’ll give it a shot.

00:33:46.440 --> 00:33:50.190
Wow, a campsite huh? Sounds neat.

00:33:50.650 --> 00:33:52.940
A locally made campsite?

00:33:54.030 --> 00:33:56.820
Sounds like a good topic for a
regular travel magazine column doesn’t it?

00:33:58.030 --> 00:34:00.830
- Eh?
- How about it boss?

00:34:02.750 --> 00:34:03.830
OK

00:34:03.910 --> 00:34:06.330
R-really？

00:34:06.420 --> 00:34:10.840
For a writer, you have to write what you know.

00:34:10.920 --> 00:34:12.590
Please submit a web version as well.

00:34:12.670 --> 00:34:15.220
Give me your proposal by end of day.

00:34:15.300 --> 00:34:17.840
Yes, sir! I’ll get right on it!

00:34:28.230 --> 00:34:29.400
Heeey!

00:34:29.480 --> 00:34:31.110
- Ah!
- There she is!

00:34:31.190 --> 00:34:32.610
- Ena!

00:34:32.690 --> 00:34:34.570
Thanks for waiting.

00:34:35.440 --> 00:34:37.360
Hey everyone, it’s been so long!

00:34:37.450 --> 00:34:39.870
- Nice to see you!
- Welcome.

00:34:39.950 --> 00:34:41.620
You seem well!

00:34:41.700 --> 00:34:45.250
Alright, everyone’s finally here.

00:34:45.330 --> 00:34:46.620
Yeah!

00:34:47.830 --> 00:34:50.630
Right behind this door,
are our operation headquarters.

00:34:53.340 --> 00:34:55.380
Th-this… this is-

00:35:00.260 --> 00:35:01.600
-so narrow！

00:35:03.890 --> 00:35:06.310
I asked them to lend me a room
for the project, and, well

00:35:06.390 --> 00:35:08.020
This is it.

00:35:08.100 --> 00:35:10.230
It looks like the old club room.

00:35:10.310 --> 00:35:11.650
Yeah!

00:35:11.730 --> 00:35:14.940
Well, it’s okay since we’ll
only use this room for meetings.

00:35:15.030 --> 00:35:16.740
This much space should be enough for that.

00:35:16.820 --> 00:35:18.280
Oops!

00:35:19.820 --> 00:35:20.820
What the heck is that?

00:35:20.910 --> 00:35:24.200
This right here is
our tourism PR robot, Jinja.

00:35:24.280 --> 00:35:26.330
Please be nice to him.

00:35:26.410 --> 00:35:28.660
Why is he here in storage?

00:35:28.750 --> 00:35:31.460
Well, he’s gone through a lot.

00:35:33.500 --> 00:35:34.920
Let’s play rock, paper, scissors!

00:35:38.380 --> 00:35:41.930
Rock… paper… scissors!

00:35:42.010 --> 00:35:44.260
And set! This is my win!

00:35:46.720 --> 00:35:49.940
I-isn’t this just a
rock, paper, scissors robot?

00:35:55.630 --> 00:35:58.630
Plan

00:35:56.650 --> 00:35:58.570
I did a little bit of research.

00:35:58.630 --> 00:36:02.260
Site Work

00:35:58.630 --> 00:36:02.260
Admin

00:35:59.070 --> 00:36:02.200
It seems like three things are
necessary for a campsite.

00:36:04.370 --> 00:36:09.200
First we need to come up with an idea of
what the campsite will be and who will come.

00:36:09.290 --> 00:36:12.080
At the same time,
we’ll be prepping the site.

00:36:12.170 --> 00:36:16.590
We’ll do this on a rotating schedule
between our day-jobs.

00:36:17.550 --> 00:36:19.460
After that comes the opening.

00:36:19.840 --> 00:36:24.050
We’ll need to make things like
an online reservation system
and operating guidelines.

00:36:24.140 --> 00:36:25.470
That makes sense!

00:36:25.550 --> 00:36:27.970
Then let’s get started with making a plan.

00:36:28.060 --> 00:36:32.600
We need to consider who this will be for and
what kind of site they’ll need.

00:36:32.690 --> 00:36:33.980
Yeah…

00:36:34.560 --> 00:36:38.110
It would be nice if it was a place
our friends and family could enjoy!

00:36:38.610 --> 00:36:41.110
It would be nice if solo travelers
could also enjoy it.

00:36:41.570 --> 00:36:45.160
A campsite that keeps children happy
would also be good.

00:36:45.240 --> 00:36:47.120
Like one with a kids’ space.

00:36:47.580 --> 00:36:48.990
If we make a dog run

00:36:49.080 --> 00:36:51.870
campers could come with their dogs!

00:36:51.960 --> 00:36:55.440
Quite a number of our customers
like to go camping.

00:36:55.920 --> 00:36:57.040
With a variety of campers

00:36:57.130 --> 00:37:00.260
It would be nice if it was a campsite
that could be enjoyed in a variety of ways.

00:37:01.880 --> 00:37:02.880
Agreed.

00:37:02.970 --> 00:37:07.300
Let’s go to the site and think
about the specifics.

00:37:07.390 --> 00:37:09.140
Why don’t we trim the grass
while we’re there?

00:37:09.640 --> 00:37:11.560
Go team!

00:37:16.150 --> 00:37:18.770
Alright, you guys, first things first.

00:37:18.860 --> 00:37:20.030
Hm?

00:37:22.400 --> 00:37:24.030
Weekend Warriors!

00:37:24.110 --> 00:37:26.780
Coverall rangers!

00:37:29.200 --> 00:37:31.200
We have gloves and tools as well.

00:37:31.290 --> 00:37:33.040
Ooh!

00:37:33.120 --> 00:37:37.000
It’s been a while since we all wore
the same clothes like in high school.

00:37:37.080 --> 00:37:39.920
- Yeah.
- It’s exciting!

00:37:40.000 --> 00:37:42.260
Hm? What’s that?

00:37:42.340 --> 00:37:44.930
I thought I’d record what we do.

00:37:45.010 --> 00:37:47.430
Maybe we could turn it into something.

00:37:47.510 --> 00:37:50.560
Ooh, good idea PR Chief.

00:37:50.850 --> 00:37:52.680
So, Ena-San!

00:37:52.770 --> 00:37:55.390
How would you describe how you’re
feeling right now?

00:37:55.480 --> 00:37:57.810
I’m going to give it my all!

00:37:57.900 --> 00:37:59.270
Ahahah~

00:37:59.360 --> 00:38:00.820
What are they doing over there?

00:38:01.530 --> 00:38:03.320
Let’s stop horsing around and get started.

00:38:03.400 --> 00:38:04.820
Okay!

00:38:15.660 --> 00:38:17.710
Huh?

00:38:17.790 --> 00:38:20.130
This grass is pretty tough.

00:38:24.590 --> 00:38:26.090
It won’t cut…

00:38:26.170 --> 00:38:28.930
This is harder than I expected.

00:38:29.010 --> 00:38:32.470
I don’t really have much experience with
cutting grass to begin with…

00:38:32.850 --> 00:38:34.100
Hm?

00:38:34.560 --> 00:38:37.640
Ugh, there’s a huge pile of garbage
back here.

00:38:38.440 --> 00:38:40.770
We’ll have to clean this too.

00:38:40.860 --> 00:38:42.480
Agreed.

00:38:43.940 --> 00:38:46.860
Ugh, my back hurts!

00:38:46.950 --> 00:38:49.740
Ugh, mine too!

00:38:50.280 --> 00:38:52.490
Rin, please take over for us.

00:38:52.580 --> 00:38:54.870
But you’ve only just started.

00:38:58.620 --> 00:39:01.630
Hey, what’s that over there?

00:39:04.960 --> 00:39:07.590
Yeah, I’ve been
wondering the same thing.

00:39:07.670 --> 00:39:09.590
That?

00:39:09.680 --> 00:39:12.300
That’s… an aviary.

00:39:12.390 --> 00:39:13.760
An aviary?

00:39:14.350 --> 00:39:15.720
When this place opened,

00:39:15.810 --> 00:39:18.640
It was intended to be a place where
you could see and meet birds.

00:39:19.020 --> 00:39:21.860
However the openings were too big…

00:39:22.900 --> 00:39:25.230
and one day the birds made a break for it.

00:39:25.320 --> 00:39:28.400
In retrospect it’s sort of a funny story.

00:39:28.700 --> 00:39:30.530
What are we going to do with it?

00:39:30.610 --> 00:39:32.780
I guess we could just get rid of it…

00:39:43.750 --> 00:39:47.550
Wow. At this rate we won’t
make much progress.

00:39:47.630 --> 00:39:49.720
Hey, little Ōgaki!

00:39:49.800 --> 00:39:50.930
Huh?

00:39:51.010 --> 00:39:53.430
Oh, Mr. Okazaki!

00:39:53.760 --> 00:39:57.180
I thought I’d bring some of the yuzu
we had at home.

00:39:57.600 --> 00:39:59.680
Amazing!

00:39:59.770 --> 00:40:01.600
Thank you so much sir!

00:40:01.690 --> 00:40:02.850
Hehe

00:40:02.940 --> 00:40:05.230
Are you all cutting grass by hand?

00:40:05.320 --> 00:40:08.440
We are but it’s not going too great.

00:40:08.940 --> 00:40:09.950
Huh…

00:40:10.030 --> 00:40:15.450
Bend it down like this and
cut near the roots.

00:40:18.540 --> 00:40:21.710
This type of saw is meant to be
pulled in order to cut.

00:40:22.040 --> 00:40:26.170
So you’ll want to hold it a little more
lightly when you’re pushing it.

00:40:26.250 --> 00:40:30.970
If you only move it a little,
you’ll get tired,
so move it from tip to handle.

00:40:31.340 --> 00:40:32.590
Amazing!

00:40:33.550 --> 00:40:35.720
Don’t hurt yourselves, okay?

00:40:36.050 --> 00:40:38.470
Thank you so much!

00:40:40.020 --> 00:40:42.230
I really learned a lot.

00:40:42.310 --> 00:40:44.150
Your neighbor?

00:40:44.230 --> 00:40:46.610
Yeah. Mr. Okazaki is a farmer.

00:40:46.690 --> 00:40:49.230
You two are pretty
buddy-buddy, aren’t you?

00:40:49.320 --> 00:40:50.610
Ehehehe

00:40:51.110 --> 00:40:54.700
I talk to the locals a lot.

00:40:54.780 --> 00:40:56.370
Of course we’ll be careful but…

00:40:56.450 --> 00:41:00.120
there is the possibility that we
could be a nuisance or a burden…

00:41:00.540 --> 00:41:04.370
But I want the people who live nearby
to also look forward to the campsite.

00:41:11.380 --> 00:41:13.840
Oh wow, it cuts so easily.

00:41:13.930 --> 00:41:15.890
It’s completely different!

00:41:34.610 --> 00:41:38.370
- Phew…
- Ooh, you’ve really cute a lot.

00:41:38.450 --> 00:41:41.830
Yeah, we’ve really made a lot of progress
on clearing stuff out.

00:41:41.910 --> 00:41:43.790
Hey everyone!

00:41:44.790 --> 00:41:47.170
Let’s call it a wrap for today.
Does anyone want some tea?

00:41:47.540 --> 00:41:49.670
Go team!

00:41:56.180 --> 00:41:58.510
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

00:41:58.600 --> 00:42:00.810
Wow, such a nice aroma.

00:42:00.890 --> 00:42:03.770
I infused it with some of the rinds
from the yuzu we ge got.

00:42:03.850 --> 00:42:05.310
（あおい）Wow~

00:42:07.940 --> 00:42:11.400
Mmph! It’s waking up my tired body.

00:42:11.480 --> 00:42:12.690
Delicious…

00:42:12.780 --> 00:42:15.860
The smell of yuzu is so calming…

00:42:17.360 --> 00:42:20.410
It’s been a long time since
we’ve been able to do something like this.

00:42:20.490 --> 00:42:25.080
This reminds me of making a
bonfire in the schoolyard and
drinking coffee together.

00:42:25.160 --> 00:42:27.210
It’s so nostalgic.

00:42:27.620 --> 00:42:32.000
We can even see Mt. Fuji from here…

00:42:32.090 --> 00:42:33.710
This really is a nice place.

00:42:34.010 --> 00:42:37.930
If you think about it, if we maintain
the turf

00:42:38.010 --> 00:42:40.390
this could be a nice place to
set down tents.

00:42:40.470 --> 00:42:45.930
Yeah! Now we just have to
incorporate all our other ideas.

00:42:46.020 --> 00:42:48.480
Let me draw a little something.

00:42:51.060 --> 00:42:54.650
If we make a solo site here,
and make a family site there,

00:42:54.730 --> 00:42:57.110
with a dog run
and a kid’s area…

00:42:57.820 --> 00:42:59.240
It would look something like this.

00:42:59.360 --> 00:43:01.490
Oooh, that’s nice.

00:43:01.570 --> 00:43:03.620
That’s a lot of stuff.

00:43:03.700 --> 00:43:06.580
I think we could clear up some space.

00:43:06.660 --> 00:43:09.170
But if we have the aviary removed

00:43:09.250 --> 00:43:15.090
and add on some playground equipment
the budget might be a little tight.

00:43:15.170 --> 00:43:17.510
- Ah…
- That’s true…

00:43:19.260 --> 00:43:24.510
We may need a campsite concept to
make all these ideas come together.

00:43:24.810 --> 00:43:26.430
A concept?

00:43:26.520 --> 00:43:29.520
Like a vision of what kind of campsite we want.

00:43:29.600 --> 00:43:31.520
Hmmm

00:43:31.600 --> 00:43:33.480
A concept…

00:43:33.570 --> 00:43:35.780
I can’t really think of one
off the top of my head.

00:43:36.190 --> 00:43:41.450
Well I’ll be going to other campsites,
so I’ll think about it for a while.

00:43:41.530 --> 00:43:42.620
Covering other camps?

00:43:42.700 --> 00:43:46.660
Yes, I was given the go ahead to write
a series about camps, including here.

00:43:46.750 --> 00:43:48.200
Eh!

00:43:48.290 --> 00:43:50.500
You should’ve said something earlier!

00:43:50.580 --> 00:43:52.170
Ah… Should I not?

00:43:52.250 --> 00:43:56.170
Of course it’s okay!
It will be the talk of the town.

00:43:56.710 --> 00:44:00.680
It’s for a local magazine in Nagoya,
so I’m not sure it will be effective PR.

00:44:00.760 --> 00:44:03.550
Still I think there will be people
who are interested.

00:44:03.680 --> 00:44:04.930
Yeah!

00:44:06.510 --> 00:44:10.940
Well, okay. I’ll do my interview next week
and then report back to everyone.

00:44:11.270 --> 00:44:12.270
Okay!

00:44:43.220 --> 00:44:46.140
Hello. I’m the Shima who
called you earlier.

00:44:46.220 --> 00:44:48.720
Ah, I’ve been waiting for you.

00:44:59.650 --> 00:45:01.740
It’s a great campsite, isn’t it?

00:45:02.240 --> 00:45:04.990
I used to come here all the time.

00:45:05.320 --> 00:45:07.990
Heh. Is that so?

00:45:12.960 --> 00:45:16.250
It feels like it hasn’t changed at all.

00:45:17.630 --> 00:45:22.130
I do my best to leave as much
of the natural scenery intact as possible.

00:45:22.130 --> 00:45:24.340
As you said, I’ve left it as is.

00:45:24.430 --> 00:45:26.260
As is…

00:45:26.680 --> 00:45:30.600
I thought that approach would
bring out the best in this place.

00:47:07.340 --> 00:47:10.050
I’ve done a lot of interviews.

00:47:11.680 --> 00:47:14.560
And I’ve been thinking
about it.                      .

00:47:14.720 --> 00:47:23.320
Maybe instead of getting rid of stuff,
we can repurpose it instead?          .

00:47:20.790 --> 00:47:22.960
We could use it instead?

00:47:23.650 --> 00:47:30.570
I think the aviary and other things, already
fit in with the place as is.              .

00:47:41.250 --> 00:47:44.800
I get that. It would be good for the
budget if we made use of it.

00:47:47.550 --> 00:47:51.340
In that case, why don’t we use the
old drums behind the building?

00:47:51.680 --> 00:47:56.100
They could be used
in the dog park!

00:47:54.050 --> 00:47:56.100
Oh, we could!

00:47:57.520 --> 00:48:00.850
It might also be a good
idea to talk with the locals.

00:48:01.020 --> 00:48:05.860
Maybe they could give
us whatever they’re not using.      .

00:48:04.230 --> 00:48:05.860
Ooh~!   .

00:48:08.780 --> 00:48:11.110
Yeah, that sounds great!

00:48:25.230 --> 00:48:27.320
Okay, let’s see if this will work.

00:48:30.700 --> 00:48:32.200
As you wish!

00:48:53.430 --> 00:48:55.050
Ah, thanks.

00:48:55.140 --> 00:48:56.890
Is that for work?

00:48:56.970 --> 00:48:58.770
Yeah… it is.

00:48:58.850 --> 00:49:00.600
You’re really going at it, huh.

00:49:02.600 --> 00:49:03.600
Maybe.

00:49:06.650 --> 00:49:09.110
Hey you two, I have apples
but they’re not pe-

00:49:09.480 --> 00:49:10.690
We’ll take ‘em.

00:49:14.990 --> 00:49:16.120
Alright.

00:49:39.760 --> 00:49:41.140
No wonder it’s cold.

00:49:50.880 --> 00:49:54.470
Hey there Rin!           .

00:49:52.300 --> 00:49:54.470
Is it snowing there?

00:49:55.300 --> 00:49:59.470
Hey there.

00:49:56.800 --> 00:49:59.470
It hasn't snowed since  .
I departed Takaori.  .

00:50:02.060 --> 00:50:06.230
Now I’m parked in Hagatake
on my way back to Nagoya.

00:50:06.560 --> 00:50:09.610
I pulled over in Dangozaka to eat.

00:50:09.940 --> 00:50:13.360
We passed each other, huh?

00:50:12.320 --> 00:50:13.360
Yeah…

00:50:16.200 --> 00:50:24.290
The options in the food court
are so fun!                .

00:50:19.700 --> 00:50:25.750
It’s really cool to try out local
food when you travel.          .

00:50:26.060 --> 00:50:27.270
エヘヘ…

00:50:28.080 --> 00:50:33.800
So you’re in Nagoya for
New Years?

00:50:30.960 --> 00:50:35.510
Yeah, I have a       l
New Year deadline.

00:50:33.960 --> 00:50:35.510
I see-   .

00:50:35.840 --> 00:50:40.510
See you next year!

00:50:37.840 --> 00:50:40.510
Drive safely, okay?!

00:50:53.130 --> 00:50:55.300
Happy New Year everyone!

00:50:55.380 --> 00:50:57.470
It’s been so long since I’ve seen
all of you!

00:50:57.800 --> 00:51:00.140
Happy New Year Akari!

00:51:00.220 --> 00:51:04.350
What a polite greeting Chibi-Inuko!

00:51:04.720 --> 00:51:05.770
Right？

00:51:05.850 --> 00:51:08.850
Give me a New Year’s gift for
good behavior, Aki!

00:51:08.940 --> 00:51:11.360
You haven’t changed at all!

00:51:11.440 --> 00:51:12.900
Eheheh.

00:51:12.980 --> 00:51:15.530
How is art school in Tokyo going?

00:51:15.610 --> 00:51:18.200
It’s been busy, but it’s fun!

00:51:18.280 --> 00:51:20.990
Happy New Year, everyone.

00:51:21.070 --> 00:51:23.830
- Ah！
- Ms. Toba！

00:51:42.850 --> 00:51:45.140
So I heard everything from my sister..

00:51:45.220 --> 00:51:48.890
How is this fabled campsite goin’?
How much do you have left to do?

00:51:49.310 --> 00:51:53.150
If the prefectural office gives us the okay
we'll officially start early this year.

00:51:53.480 --> 00:51:54.900
Eh-

00:51:54.980 --> 00:51:57.440
Let me know if I can help!

00:51:57.530 --> 00:51:58.900
Will do!

00:51:58.990 --> 00:52:02.200
How about you design the
campsite logo?

00:52:02.280 --> 00:52:03.700
Nice idea!

00:52:03.780 --> 00:52:06.990
Inuyama, you’re at
Fujikawa Elementary,right?

00:52:07.080 --> 00:52:08.450
I heard that in March…

00:52:08.540 --> 00:52:11.540
Ah, so you know, huh?

00:52:12.000 --> 00:52:15.040
That sounds hard.
Thank you for all your work there.

00:52:16.750 --> 00:52:18.300
Thank you so much.

00:52:18.710 --> 00:52:21.050
Hey Ms. Toba, how about
we drink next time?

00:52:21.130 --> 00:52:24.010
I’ve found a shop with
a premium sake collection.

00:52:24.100 --> 00:52:25.810
Eh? We should absolutely go.

00:52:26.140 --> 00:52:28.890
It‘s down in Kōfu but the
snacks there are worth it.

00:52:28.980 --> 00:52:30.560
Wow! Sounds great!

00:53:20.780 --> 00:53:23.360
Let’s go, everyone! Our first work day of the New Year.

00:53:25.570 --> 00:53:27.120
Weekday Squadron!

00:53:27.200 --> 00:53:30.120
Coverall Rangers!

00:53:31.370 --> 00:53:34.620
It feels a little different on a weekday.

00:53:35.540 --> 00:53:37.630
For today, let’s focus on mowing.

00:53:37.920 --> 00:53:40.880
By the way, when is our opening date?

00:53:40.960 --> 00:53:43.090
Oh, good question!

00:53:43.170 --> 00:53:44.630
In July of this year!

00:53:47.220 --> 00:53:48.640
Eh!!

00:53:49.140 --> 00:53:51.020
We only have half a year?

00:53:51.100 --> 00:53:53.390
It’s a complicated, adult, situation!

00:53:53.480 --> 00:53:56.650
It was the date given to us
after our application!

00:53:56.980 --> 00:53:58.560
Aki…

00:54:01.070 --> 00:54:03.400
Got it! We’ll make it through somehow!

00:54:03.600 --> 00:54:05.600
Next week…

00:54:10.740 --> 00:54:12.620
An excavator!

00:54:13.290 --> 00:54:15.790
Alright, I’m going in!

00:54:22.760 --> 00:54:25.680
- Ooh!
- You’re amazing Nadeshiko!

00:54:26.470 --> 00:54:29.930
I’m officially certified,
so leave it to me!

00:54:30.010 --> 00:54:33.180
Alright, we’ll get started too!

00:54:36.980 --> 00:54:38.940
An electric mower!

00:54:39.020 --> 00:54:41.440
Courtesy of Okazaki!

00:54:44.320 --> 00:54:46.490
With this
I’ll cut all of you down to size!

00:54:58.090 --> 00:54:59.900
Nadeshiko is so cool!

00:55:00.690 --> 00:55:06.780
Aki won’t back down!

00:55:03.690 --> 00:55:06.780
Things are going way
faster than I thought!

00:55:07.840 --> 00:55:10.220
Things are really shaping up…

00:55:11.420 --> 00:55:14.790
Leave some for me!

00:55:15.810 --> 00:55:19.480
Here is a review of
how to make a campsite.

00:55:19.940 --> 00:55:21.980
First, mow the grass

00:55:22.060 --> 00:55:24.480
For large areas use a mower

00:55:25.030 --> 00:55:27.990
and for smaller areas do it by hand.

00:55:30.360 --> 00:55:33.240
Besides that, use an excavator
to level the land

00:55:33.910 --> 00:55:36.620
and repair any broken stairs.

00:55:39.500 --> 00:55:43.130
Renovate the original visitor center.

00:55:46.340 --> 00:55:48.130
Get very hungry.

00:55:49.430 --> 00:55:51.340
Schedule appropriately.

00:55:57.770 --> 00:56:00.100
Plan out activities.

00:56:03.400 --> 00:56:05.610
Get the water running

00:56:08.940 --> 00:56:10.990
and things like that.

00:56:20.730 --> 00:56:23.730
How interesting! I want to see it when it’s done!

00:56:20.730 --> 00:56:23.730
Everyone’s having so much fun!

00:56:20.730 --> 00:56:23.730
This is a bit far but I’d love to go!

00:56:20.730 --> 00:56:23.730
This seems tough but you all are giving it your all!

00:56:40.640 --> 00:56:41.770
Aki!

00:56:41.850 --> 00:56:44.690
- Aki, get over here!
- Huh?

00:56:44.770 --> 00:56:46.690
Our food!

00:56:47.320 --> 00:56:48.690
And the trash!

00:56:49.570 --> 00:56:51.200
They’ve been ravaged.

00:56:53.240 --> 00:56:56.080
Does some wild animal live nearby?

00:56:56.160 --> 00:56:57.740
Because we’re near mountains

00:56:57.830 --> 00:57:00.700
deer, boars and even monkeys
are normal for this area.

00:57:01.080 --> 00:57:05.000
We’ll have to take steps to figure out
what we’re dealing with.

00:57:05.080 --> 00:57:07.250
But if there’s a wild boar around

00:57:07.340 --> 00:57:09.710
wouldn’t that be dangerous for us?

00:57:14.010 --> 00:57:17.470
There is someone up for the task!

00:57:34.820 --> 00:57:38.030
So this video feed
is Jinja is seeing?

00:57:38.120 --> 00:57:39.120
Yep

00:57:39.200 --> 00:57:42.450
I was hoping we could lure it out

00:57:46.630 --> 00:57:48.380
Ah, something’s there!

00:57:50.500 --> 00:57:52.630
Let’s play!

00:57:53.050 --> 00:57:56.260
Rock… pape-

00:57:59.720 --> 00:58:01.640
Jinja!!

00:58:01.720 --> 00:58:04.270
Be careful!

00:58:19.990 --> 00:58:22.450
It was just a tanuki family!

00:58:22.540 --> 00:58:25.290
I’m just glad it’s not a boar.

00:58:25.710 --> 00:58:29.040
For now, we’ll need to make sure we

00:58:29.130 --> 00:58:30.920
don't leave any food out.

00:58:31.750 --> 00:58:34.420
This is my win~

00:58:59.870 --> 00:59:01.700
Rin!

00:59:04.540 --> 00:59:06.210
Come on!

00:59:28.980 --> 00:59:31.400
We’ve come pretty far, huh?

00:59:31.480 --> 00:59:32.730
Yeah…

00:59:32.790 --> 00:59:36.050
Kids Area
Under Construction

00:59:36.050 --> 00:59:39.300
Proposed Dog Run Site

00:59:43.240 --> 00:59:46.250
- Rin, something’s coming this way!
- Huh？

00:59:48.620 --> 00:59:50.750
It’s… it can’t be, it’s...

00:59:52.380 --> 00:59:55.630
It’s Chikuwa!!

01:00:06.140 --> 01:00:07.890
He got overexcited.

01:00:08.270 --> 01:00:10.940
Chikuwa’s now a grandpa.

01:00:12.480 --> 01:00:15.320
Alright, looks like everyone's here.

01:00:16.860 --> 01:00:19.190
What we have here will be our "luggage."

01:00:20.360 --> 01:00:24.410
And so, let's start the first official
test-camp for the new site!

01:00:24.490 --> 01:00:26.660
Let's do it!

01:00:28.660 --> 01:00:29.710
So, Nadeshiko and I

01:00:29.790 --> 01:00:32.370
rented out this tent.

01:00:32.460 --> 01:00:35.040
Eeh, I didn't even know you could do that.

01:00:37.500 --> 01:00:38.510
It's huge!

01:00:38.590 --> 01:00:41.180
It's this big so we can all sleep in it.

01:00:41.550 --> 01:00:44.430
- Frame assembly is all done!
- Got it.

01:00:53.020 --> 01:00:55.440
There we go

01:00:56.230 --> 01:00:58.440
The tent is all ready!

01:00:58.530 --> 01:01:01.450
- Somehow we got it together.
- Yeah.

01:01:01.530 --> 01:01:04.950
We're losing daylight so let's get to the rest of it.

01:01:16.710 --> 01:01:17.710
Okay.

01:01:17.800 --> 01:01:20.590
Shall we go with this, then, Aoi?

01:01:20.670 --> 01:01:24.390
Alrighty, we're both in this together.

01:01:30.310 --> 01:01:32.770
Rin, does this look alright?

01:01:32.850 --> 01:01:34.100
It does.

01:01:44.740 --> 01:01:47.870
Zoomy zoomy!

01:01:47.950 --> 01:01:49.410
We're back!

01:01:49.490 --> 01:01:51.370
We're all done with our shopping.

01:01:51.450 --> 01:01:53.120
Welcome back~

01:01:53.210 --> 01:01:56.130
Oh! It's all nice and set up.

01:01:57.460 --> 01:01:59.800
The ingredients are
okay and ready to go!

01:01:59.880 --> 01:02:01.130
Uh-huh.

01:02:01.210 --> 01:02:04.130
Ah, I forgot to bring over the hot pot.

01:02:04.220 --> 01:02:07.640
- Aki I can carry over the
rest of the stuff!
- Thanks!

01:02:08.680 --> 01:02:11.430
Ah! A wood burning stove!

01:02:13.480 --> 01:02:16.940
This is another rental
from the store I work at.

01:02:17.020 --> 01:02:18.400
How cool!

01:02:27.660 --> 01:02:29.530
Maybe we could use the swing from the school...

01:02:30.410 --> 01:02:33.200
... like they'd let us have it.

01:02:44.750 --> 01:02:46.180
You will do.

01:02:46.400 --> 01:02:47.740
Hey there!

01:02:51.370 --> 01:02:52.490
That's hot!

01:03:13.540 --> 01:03:14.950
Tonight's meal is...

01:03:15.500 --> 01:03:17.040
this!

01:03:17.120 --> 01:03:18.960
Salmon!

01:03:19.040 --> 01:03:21.790
That's a lot of salmon, isn't it?

01:03:21.880 --> 01:03:24.460
We got a great bargain.

01:03:25.380 --> 01:03:28.220
So today we'll have a
Salmon Festival!!

01:03:29.220 --> 01:03:31.970
How to make salmon soup

01:03:32.510 --> 01:03:34.890
First, bring your water to a boil.

01:03:34.970 --> 01:03:37.980
Then introduce some pepper and bay leaf.

01:03:38.310 --> 01:03:41.730
Add some chopped onions and carrots.

01:03:42.060 --> 01:03:46.110
After a little bit
add some potatoes too.

01:03:46.190 --> 01:03:48.990
Then please wait while
it simmers for a while.

01:03:49.450 --> 01:03:52.370
I can't wait to see how it turns out!

01:03:57.660 --> 01:04:01.170
I'll just have some sake glazed salmon...

01:04:07.840 --> 01:04:09.260
When did she...

01:04:09.340 --> 01:04:12.010
She could be a sister
to our old teacher.

01:04:14.720 --> 01:04:17.140
throw in your salmon, the star of the show.

01:04:17.390 --> 01:04:20.140
throw in your salmon, the star of the show.

01:04:20.520 --> 01:04:23.900
Now just add some cream, salt

01:04:24.440 --> 01:04:26.650
and some dill, if you have it.

01:04:27.190 --> 01:04:29.900
The salmon soup is ready to eat!

01:04:31.990 --> 01:04:33.910
Thank you for the food!

01:04:41.370 --> 01:04:42.790
It's so good!

01:04:42.870 --> 01:04:45.540
Nice and warm...

01:04:45.630 --> 01:04:48.920
Delicious, it's so simple yet so rich.

01:04:49.010 --> 01:04:50.920
Heh, I'm glad!

01:04:51.260 --> 01:04:53.430
The umami of the salmon and vegetables...

01:04:53.510 --> 01:04:56.930
with the fresh cream it blends into a gentle broth.

01:05:00.350 --> 01:05:02.440
So good!

01:05:03.230 --> 01:05:05.900
I even made Chikuwa his own portion!

01:05:05.980 --> 01:05:07.940
Thanks so much Nadeshiko!

01:05:08.230 --> 01:05:10.900
There's something amazing
about how it smells.

01:05:10.990 --> 01:05:12.320
That would be the dill!

01:05:12.650 --> 01:05:14.320
It's a type of herb!

01:05:14.410 --> 01:05:15.570
Huh!

01:05:15.950 --> 01:05:18.830
The smell of the dill goes
perfectly with the salmon.

01:05:18.910 --> 01:05:23.120
It really tastes like it came straight
from a forest in Finland, right?

01:05:23.210 --> 01:05:24.420
What does that even taste like?

01:05:28.880 --> 01:05:31.090
What the, it's already all gone!

01:05:31.590 --> 01:05:33.930
Five people makes it go fast, huh.

01:05:34.010 --> 01:05:37.640
Pffft... Aki, it's not over yet.

01:05:39.970 --> 01:05:42.310
I guess it's about time to bring
bring out the second half.

01:05:45.600 --> 01:05:48.610
- A second hot pot?
- Where did that come from?

01:05:48.690 --> 01:05:52.860
He he he, the Salmon Festival
has only begun.

01:05:53.320 --> 01:05:55.700
Salmon ishikari with tofu skins!

01:05:55.780 --> 01:05:57.620
Ooh!

01:06:02.120 --> 01:06:04.370
Mmm, delishous.

01:06:07.420 --> 01:06:09.880
The miso flavor in
this one is so relaxing.

01:06:10.170 --> 01:06:13.630
The ishitari and the
tofu skins go together surprisingly well!

01:06:13.920 --> 01:06:16.720
We got some nices ones from Minobu's!

01:06:16.800 --> 01:06:19.640
I also added milk and butter so that
the flavors would go together better.

01:06:20.010 --> 01:06:22.020
That's why it's nice and mellow!

01:06:22.430 --> 01:06:24.690
Lastly, the noodles are hōtō .

01:06:24.770 --> 01:06:25.770
Yay!

01:06:25.850 --> 01:06:28.900
That's our Aoi, you're so good
at putting things together.

01:06:32.070 --> 01:06:37.070
I knew the food we'd make at our own
campsite would taste twice as good.

01:06:37.160 --> 01:06:39.070
Well it's not finished yet.

01:06:39.830 --> 01:06:45.210
However, camping here
feels truly indulgent.

01:06:45.710 --> 01:06:46.870
Agreed.

01:06:48.000 --> 01:06:51.880
It's hard work, no doubt...
but we can do it if we try.

01:06:51.960 --> 01:06:53.170
Yeah!

01:07:09.020 --> 01:07:10.900
Ena, is black coffee okay?

01:07:10.980 --> 01:07:12.690
Yeah, thank you.

01:07:13.280 --> 01:07:16.320
Maybe it's about time to start coming up
with campsite guidelines.

01:07:16.700 --> 01:07:18.660
I've been thinking it over a bit.

01:07:18.740 --> 01:07:20.320
As expected from Nadeshiko.

01:07:20.410 --> 01:07:22.580
And I was just thinking...

01:07:22.660 --> 01:07:25.830
It's a bit of a walk to
the bathroom isn't it?

01:07:25.910 --> 01:07:27.460
Ah, that's true.

01:07:27.830 --> 01:07:31.330
There's also some bumps in the main road.
They almost tripped me!

01:07:31.710 --> 01:07:35.510
It would be tough carrying stuff
up and down all those stairs.

01:07:35.590 --> 01:07:37.010
But if we rented out carts

01:07:37.090 --> 01:07:39.550
maybe it would be easier if it was a ramp.

01:07:39.630 --> 01:07:42.550
It seems like there's still much to do.

01:07:48.690 --> 01:07:51.480
Hey... would you guys want to
go check it out?

01:08:04.620 --> 01:08:09.500
Just as I expected...
it feels like a planetarium.

01:08:09.960 --> 01:08:12.040
It feels otherworldy, doesn't it?

01:08:12.130 --> 01:08:14.000
It really does...

01:08:14.590 --> 01:08:19.010
Though there are challenges, maybe with
some ingenuity we can overcome them.

01:08:23.850 --> 01:08:25.680
She might've partied too hard...

01:08:28.680 --> 01:08:30.560
Hey Chikuwa!

01:08:30.640 --> 01:08:34.310
Hm? What have you got there?

01:08:38.820 --> 01:08:40.450
I wonder what it could be?

01:08:40.530 --> 01:08:42.950
A piece of a pot... maybe?

01:08:43.030 --> 01:08:45.660
Maybe it's more
important than we think.

01:08:45.740 --> 01:08:48.040
If that's so, then great job Chikuwa!

01:09:50.600 --> 01:09:53.230
The next step is setting up the dog run.

01:09:53.310 --> 01:09:55.850
Could it really be this easy?

01:09:56.610 --> 01:09:59.150
Aoi, a word please.

01:09:59.940 --> 01:10:01.320
Ah, yes sir.

01:10:04.780 --> 01:10:05.820
Eh?

01:10:14.410 --> 01:10:15.710
I'm headed out!

01:10:15.790 --> 01:10:17.290
Have a good day!

01:10:25.590 --> 01:10:26.680
What's up?

01:10:26.760 --> 01:10:28.090
Well the thing is...

01:10:28.180 --> 01:10:31.640
There's going to be an official survey
of the land the campsite is on.

01:10:31.720 --> 01:10:34.140
Ah... a survey?

01:10:34.560 --> 01:10:36.770
That thing that Chikuwa found...

01:10:36.850 --> 01:10:41.400
I reported it to my boss just to be safe
and, well, it looks like it might be real
historical earthenware.

01:10:41.730 --> 01:10:43.030
Earthenware？

01:10:43.320 --> 01:10:46.820
Yamanashi is a pretty good place
to find historical artifcats.

01:10:46.910 --> 01:10:48.240
Is that so?

01:10:48.320 --> 01:10:52.870
But I heard it will be a week or two
at the most.

01:10:52.950 --> 01:10:55.960
Well then, when that's done we can
get back to it, right?

01:10:56.040 --> 01:10:57.040
Yep!

01:10:57.540 --> 01:10:59.670
I guess we'll just take
it easy untill then.

01:10:59.750 --> 01:11:04.300
Okay, I'll get back to you
as soon as I know more.

01:11:04.970 --> 01:11:07.840
In the meantime, though,
take it easy okay?

01:11:07.930 --> 01:11:11.510
Alright, sounds good. Bye then.

01:11:16.890 --> 01:11:19.690
Eh? You want to do
that on top of everything else you have?

01:11:19.770 --> 01:11:25.320
Well... it's been a while since I've been
able to go and say "hi" to the printer.

01:11:25.610 --> 01:11:29.570
Don't you have too much on your plate?
Maybe you could give Rin some of it?

01:11:31.570 --> 01:11:36.450
I'd prefer to do it myself.

01:11:37.830 --> 01:11:40.290
Maybe now is a good time to just push myself.

01:11:41.840 --> 01:11:43.210
Mr. Kariya!

01:11:43.710 --> 01:11:45.420
Don't tell me you overheard?

01:11:45.510 --> 01:11:47.970
Take me with you to the printer!

01:11:48.050 --> 01:11:49.970
Well... but...

01:11:50.470 --> 01:11:53.220
I'm not going to Yamanashi today.

01:11:54.260 --> 01:11:56.350
Is that so...

01:12:00.560 --> 01:12:03.480
There you go, good boy!

01:12:03.900 --> 01:12:06.320
Wait here until I come back, okay?

01:12:12.870 --> 01:12:15.200
Yeah, okay.

01:12:15.290 --> 01:12:17.750
I'm not going to Takaori today.

01:12:19.160 --> 01:12:20.960
So I'll go directly home.

01:12:46.270 --> 01:12:49.610
Ah, Aoi, see you later!

01:12:49.690 --> 01:12:52.280
I'm not "Aoi" I'm your teacher!

01:12:53.990 --> 01:12:56.530
Bye Aoi1

01:13:47.590 --> 01:13:49.000
Hey!

01:13:49.710 --> 01:13:51.880
S-so...

01:13:53.470 --> 01:13:54.880
It turns out...

01:13:55.430 --> 01:13:59.930
That earthenware appears to date
back to the Jōmon period.

01:14:01.180 --> 01:14:02.890
In order to excavate...

01:14:02.980 --> 01:14:06.440
The site will be off limits for months.

01:14:07.230 --> 01:14:09.610
But then after that it will be open, right?

01:14:09.690 --> 01:14:11.230
Well, that's not...

01:14:12.190 --> 01:14:14.740
They've found quite a few artifacts already...

01:14:14.820 --> 01:14:19.490
and because of that they're considering
turning it into a historical site.

01:14:19.950 --> 01:14:21.240
Eh?

01:14:22.250 --> 01:14:24.040
We'll have to stop making the campsite.

01:14:24.120 --> 01:14:28.130
The prefecture has decided to rethink
what is going to happen to that area.

01:14:30.300 --> 01:14:34.130
Is there any chance the plan
for the campground could come back?

01:14:34.220 --> 01:14:37.800
Historical ruins? That's sure to get
folks invested in the place.

01:14:37.890 --> 01:14:40.010
So, unfortunately, it's unlikely.

01:14:40.760 --> 01:14:42.060
Ah...

01:14:42.140 --> 01:14:44.270
I know everyone put in a ton
of effort over there.

01:14:44.770 --> 01:14:46.270
I'm truly sorry!

01:15:28.380 --> 01:15:33.500
Kajisawa Fujimi Elementary School
Closing Ceremony

01:15:38.720 --> 01:15:43.560
"Thanks for everything!"

01:15:59.550 --> 01:16:00.840
Hey there!

01:16:05.010 --> 01:16:06.140
Is this everything?

01:16:06.220 --> 01:16:08.480
Yep, thanks for the help.

01:16:17.990 --> 01:16:19.740
I heard they're tearing it down?

01:16:19.820 --> 01:16:21.990
What will happen is still being discussed.

01:16:22.490 --> 01:16:23.870
Oh...

01:16:30.080 --> 01:16:33.420
Ow! What was that for?

01:16:35.460 --> 01:16:37.510
Good job, Inuko.

01:16:40.680 --> 01:16:42.930
Thank you...

01:16:43.010 --> 01:16:46.850
but I'm not quitting teaching,
just so you know.

01:16:46.930 --> 01:16:50.020
I'm just relocating to a new school.

01:16:54.900 --> 01:16:57.780
Still... it's sad.

01:17:11.660 --> 01:17:13.040
Whatever.

01:17:13.540 --> 01:17:15.960
I'm just kiddin'.

01:17:19.710 --> 01:17:21.550
You!

01:17:21.630 --> 01:17:23.550
How dare you deceive me!

01:17:23.630 --> 01:17:26.100
- Hehehe.... no~!
- Hey! Wait! Hey!

01:17:26.180 --> 01:17:30.810
- Wait, Aki, it's raining!
- This is what happens when you lie!

01:17:36.230 --> 01:17:37.980
I'm back!

01:17:39.150 --> 01:17:42.150
So you know what the car sounds like?

01:17:42.900 --> 01:17:46.910
Yes, yes. So you want to go for a walk?

01:17:59.900 --> 01:18:02.990
"Let's Make a Campsite!" series to end
due to unforeseen events

01:18:06.180 --> 01:18:07.470
It's submitted.

01:18:07.550 --> 01:18:09.600
Hm? Okay.

01:18:10.470 --> 01:18:12.480
Good work!

01:18:12.560 --> 01:18:14.350
- Um...
- Hmm?

01:18:14.940 --> 01:18:17.110
Is there anything else I can do?

01:18:17.610 --> 01:18:20.400
Why don't you go home?
Yesterday you had to go home late, right?

01:18:20.480 --> 01:18:23.030
It's okay. I want to do my share of the work.

01:18:23.110 --> 01:18:25.110
I wouldn't say you haven-

01:18:25.530 --> 01:18:27.450
I said it's okay.

01:18:29.240 --> 01:18:33.620
Well then, could I ask you to look over
the manuscript for the new publication?

01:18:33.700 --> 01:18:34.830
Yes sir.

01:18:40.130 --> 01:18:42.340
- Thank you, sir.
- Sure.

01:19:20.170 --> 01:19:22.590
- Kagamihara.
- Ah, yes?

01:19:22.670 --> 01:19:26.130
Could you put out the issues of
"Bivouac" that just came in?

01:19:26.220 --> 01:19:27.800
On it!

01:19:31.850 --> 01:19:34.220
It really is costly...

01:19:35.600 --> 01:19:37.810
As I said you should just get a candle.

01:19:37.890 --> 01:19:39.810
Like some kind of occult ritual?

01:19:41.980 --> 01:19:44.320
Those... those girls.

01:19:45.780 --> 01:19:47.820
- Excuse me.
- Hm?

01:19:48.450 --> 01:19:50.240
Are you looking for something?

01:19:51.740 --> 01:19:55.620
We were thinking of going camping
to celebrate graduation...

01:19:55.700 --> 01:20:00.080
but we weren't really sure what to bring.

01:20:00.170 --> 01:20:03.340
There's a lot of tools
and a lot of them are expensive.

01:20:05.840 --> 01:20:08.720
Given this is your first time
you don't have to spend the night.

01:20:08.800 --> 01:20:10.970
You could even just do a picnic.

01:20:11.050 --> 01:20:15.100
Or maybe make a fire and cook something
ready-to-eat. It's always nice to eat.

01:20:16.470 --> 01:20:17.730
Even just that's okay?

01:20:17.810 --> 01:20:18.850
Of course!

01:20:19.270 --> 01:20:20.730
Anything goes.

01:20:20.810 --> 01:20:23.610
You can pick up the tool later,
little by little.

01:20:25.940 --> 01:20:28.280
So, would you guys want to
eat some cup ramen?

01:20:28.360 --> 01:20:30.320
I think you just want to eat.

01:20:30.400 --> 01:20:31.780
I'll take seafood flavor!

01:20:31.860 --> 01:20:34.700
I think mine will be
plain old shoyu.

01:20:34.780 --> 01:20:36.370
Then I'll go with tonkotsu.

01:20:36.450 --> 01:20:39.910
Hahaha What is up tonkotsu flavor?
It's so hard to find!

01:20:40.000 --> 01:20:41.870
- It's so annoying!
- Hahaha...

01:20:48.630 --> 01:20:50.630
Thank you for stopping by!

01:20:54.180 --> 01:20:55.890
What's going on?

01:20:56.640 --> 01:21:00.640
They reminded me of when I
first started camping.

01:21:01.690 --> 01:21:03.850
I hope they have fun.

01:21:08.440 --> 01:21:11.900
I knew you were suited for this job,
Kagamihara.

01:22:00.040 --> 01:22:03.460
What the! Hm?

01:22:04.290 --> 01:22:05.270
Yo!

01:22:05.270 --> 01:22:06.650
<b>Yo!!</b>

01:22:10.590 --> 01:22:13.590
Hey... now you're easier to eat.

01:22:13.920 --> 01:22:15.890
Well I'm going to go take a break.

01:22:15.970 --> 01:22:18.100
Eh? Mr. Koriya?

01:22:18.470 --> 01:22:21.850
Well Shima, looks like I'll have to
give you more work.

01:22:21.930 --> 01:22:24.140
Ah, editor in chief?

01:22:25.100 --> 01:22:28.150
It's really okay!
I'll do anything you ask!

01:22:31.730 --> 01:22:34.110
Rin, it's all ready!

01:22:34.200 --> 01:22:36.450
Our campsite...

01:22:37.740 --> 01:22:41.410
is finally complete!

01:22:43.450 --> 01:22:45.620
♪ Tsuka Tsuka Tsukapon ♪

01:22:45.710 --> 01:22:47.000
Amazing!

01:22:47.710 --> 01:22:49.340
Looks like you're having fun!

01:22:49.420 --> 01:22:50.500
Eh?

01:22:50.590 --> 01:22:52.920
Shima, get going to your interview!

01:22:53.010 --> 01:22:54.260
Wait, what, interview?

01:22:54.340 --> 01:22:56.510
Well, off you go!

01:23:00.100 --> 01:23:03.020
Safe travels!

01:23:03.930 --> 01:23:05.390
Everyone...

01:23:05.480 --> 01:23:08.770
I'm really...
I'm really grateful for this.

01:23:09.190 --> 01:23:11.190
Alright, I'm on my way!

01:23:29.880 --> 01:23:31.250
What even was that?

01:23:34.090 --> 01:23:37.130
（配達員）Ms. Shima? Are you there?
It's a delivery!

01:23:37.220 --> 01:23:40.550
Oh, yes, my apologies!

01:23:45.350 --> 01:23:49.310
Rin,
Are you eating?
Here are some emergency rations.

01:23:49.310 --> 01:23:52.400
Please take care.
Love,
Mom

01:23:55.900 --> 01:23:57.570
Emergency rations...

01:24:06.940 --> 01:24:10.750
Hey Rin! Would you want to
go to a hot spring soon?     .

01:24:11.790 --> 01:24:14.670
A... hot spring?!

01:24:36.440 --> 01:24:40.110
This isn't a trip to the hot springs,
it's more like mountain climbing.

01:24:40.610 --> 01:24:42.870
Rin, you can do it!

01:24:43.320 --> 01:24:46.870
After all that climbing these
hot springs will be amazing!

01:24:51.330 --> 01:24:54.290
This part isn't so bad...

01:24:54.380 --> 01:24:56.380
I think I've been at this for an hour.

01:24:57.420 --> 01:25:00.380
I see you're not tired at all, Nadeshiko.

01:25:00.470 --> 01:25:02.640
I have so much energy I could sell it!

01:25:02.720 --> 01:25:05.850
Sell it to me, now.

01:25:19.650 --> 01:25:21.030
（飼い主）Hello.

01:25:21.110 --> 01:25:22.400
Hi there.

01:25:29.330 --> 01:25:32.830
Mmhm, nice and slow.

01:25:47.930 --> 01:25:50.100
It feels nice to lay there, huh?

01:25:51.270 --> 01:25:56.190
When we were at campsite,
you were so excitable.

01:26:09.620 --> 01:26:11.410
You're so nice and warm...

01:26:25.800 --> 01:26:28.640
That startled me...

01:26:28.720 --> 01:26:29.720
Hello?

01:26:30.430 --> 01:26:31.850
Hey, Inuko.

01:26:33.230 --> 01:26:35.230
So, I...

01:26:46.610 --> 01:26:48.780
- There you go.
- Thanks.

01:26:50.370 --> 01:26:52.120
Seafood flavor today, hmm?

01:26:52.200 --> 01:26:57.750
Yesterday some high school girls came in
and were talking about

01:26:57.920 --> 01:27:00.920
what flavor of cup noodles they liked.

01:27:02.380 --> 01:27:05.590
I thought it would be nice to
try something different.

01:27:05.670 --> 01:27:07.640
Is curry still your favorite?

01:27:12.310 --> 01:27:13.390
It is.

01:27:17.900 --> 01:27:19.520
Let's dig in!

01:27:19.610 --> 01:27:21.020
Thank you for the food.

01:27:49.180 --> 01:27:50.550
Oh, yeah!

01:27:51.260 --> 01:27:52.680
I brought some onigiri too.

01:27:53.890 --> 01:27:55.060
Here, take one.

01:27:55.140 --> 01:27:56.430
It's huge...

01:28:04.820 --> 01:28:06.540
From here we'll need a little more grip...

01:28:06.570 --> 01:28:07.570
Okay.

01:28:48.070 --> 01:28:50.420
Honzawa hot springs, this way.

01:29:07.190 --> 01:29:12.700
Honzawa hot spring, a hidden gem of Japan.
Japan's highest open-air hot spring.

01:29:20.350 --> 01:29:23.060
Phew, we're finally here.

01:29:23.150 --> 01:29:27.150
We can buy tickets here.
The bath is a little further ahead.

01:29:27.860 --> 01:29:30.150
Still more climbing?

01:29:33.530 --> 01:29:36.490
My sister told me about this place.

01:29:36.580 --> 01:29:37.660
Sakura?

01:29:38.540 --> 01:29:40.160
She called me the other day.

01:29:40.620 --> 01:29:43.460
I told her about what
happened with the campsite.

01:29:43.540 --> 01:29:44.550
And so...

01:29:44.940 --> 01:29:48.230
If you have the time,
might as well go here?

01:29:49.400 --> 01:29:51.110
Yatsugatake Yumoto Honzawa Onsen

01:29:49.400 --> 01:29:51.110
An open air bath in the tallest place in Japan

01:29:53.200 --> 01:29:55.620
It was on a show I saw.

01:29:55.930 --> 01:29:57.180
... so yeah!

01:29:58.260 --> 01:30:00.310
That sounds like her.

01:30:00.510 --> 01:30:02.870
Open-air bath

01:30:06.560 --> 01:30:08.320
Ooh!

01:30:17.740 --> 01:30:19.370
What an amazing view!

01:30:19.450 --> 01:30:20.580
Yeah...

01:30:20.660 --> 01:30:23.080
Oh, the hot spring is down there!

01:30:23.460 --> 01:30:25.580
Eh! It's tiny!

01:30:26.170 --> 01:30:29.090
On top of that it's right there on the slope.

01:30:29.170 --> 01:30:31.260
Right out in the open!

01:30:31.340 --> 01:30:33.760
Where even is the changing room?

01:30:33.840 --> 01:30:36.180
- We can just undress right here.
- What?

01:30:36.260 --> 01:30:38.550
There's no one here, it will be fine.

01:30:49.860 --> 01:30:53.440
All the fatigue in my body is melting away...

01:30:53.530 --> 01:30:56.070
It really is~

01:30:58.240 --> 01:31:00.450
The thing about hot springs is...

01:31:00.530 --> 01:31:01.950
Hm?

01:31:02.040 --> 01:31:06.040
the older you get the better they feel.

01:31:06.120 --> 01:31:07.880
They really do...

01:31:09.920 --> 01:31:13.340
We're really adults now...

01:31:14.550 --> 01:31:18.300
We both have jobs
and more money to spend

01:31:18.680 --> 01:31:21.140
and I've been able to buy
lots more camping gear.

01:31:21.760 --> 01:31:23.930
You even got your license.

01:31:24.020 --> 01:31:25.270
Yeah!

01:31:25.350 --> 01:31:28.400
I can just jump in the car and go
to Tokyo or Yamanashi!

01:31:29.020 --> 01:31:32.230
The long ago days of bike-bound Nadeshiko...

01:31:32.320 --> 01:31:35.650
Eheh. Now I'm a real member of society.

01:31:39.110 --> 01:31:40.240
But...

01:31:40.870 --> 01:31:43.910
even as an adult there
are some things I can't do.

01:31:47.370 --> 01:31:50.080
Takaori was really fun...

01:31:50.670 --> 01:31:52.290
There's just something
about that place.

01:31:52.380 --> 01:31:55.210
It was like we were on a
months long camping trip.

01:31:56.510 --> 01:31:58.930
Before it came along

01:31:59.010 --> 01:32:02.470
I would think over and over
about seeing everyone again.

01:32:04.810 --> 01:32:08.810
And then that camp
brought us together again.

01:32:11.610 --> 01:32:14.320
I was thinking the same thing.

01:32:15.280 --> 01:32:20.070
Though I feel like, because of the camp
I've created more work for my coworkers...

01:32:20.160 --> 01:32:22.320
I know I've been a burden on them.

01:32:22.410 --> 01:32:23.910
Did you tick them off?

01:32:23.990 --> 01:32:27.830
No... they've been supportive all the way.

01:32:28.710 --> 01:32:33.090
I just had believed that when I grew up
I could do whatever.

01:32:33.880 --> 01:32:37.420
But in reality, what you would call responsibilities...

01:32:37.510 --> 01:32:40.300
The things I needed to do, piled
up higher and higher

01:32:40.760 --> 01:32:43.050
But in the end, even now that I'm older

01:32:43.140 --> 01:32:46.100
I've been propped up by the support
of those around me.

01:32:46.430 --> 01:32:50.020
I've realized that I'm not all by myself.

01:32:50.730 --> 01:32:53.860
Huh... I can get that.

01:33:05.660 --> 01:33:08.700
Even still, though...

01:33:08.790 --> 01:33:13.130
There are things I can do
now I couldn't previously.

01:33:14.630 --> 01:33:15.630
Like what?

01:33:16.880 --> 01:33:17.880
For example...

01:33:19.090 --> 01:33:20.840
What we're doing now,

01:33:20.920 --> 01:33:24.800
The things we enjoy and care about,
will impact and be shared with others.

01:33:26.220 --> 01:33:31.230
And those people will pass on the fun,
and then those people will pass it on.

01:33:34.230 --> 01:33:35.440
Something like that.

01:33:35.520 --> 01:33:38.690
A place full of possibilities...

01:33:42.610 --> 01:33:47.160
A place full of possibilities...

01:33:49.240 --> 01:33:51.750
If I could do that... that would be truly amazing.

01:33:53.250 --> 01:33:56.590
If I could do that... that would be truly amazing.

01:33:56.670 --> 01:33:58.170
You can!

01:33:58.500 --> 01:34:00.800
Because it was you, Rin,

01:34:00.880 --> 01:34:04.300
who first taught me to love camping!

01:34:07.600 --> 01:34:08.680
That's all?

01:34:08.760 --> 01:34:11.270
- Am I forgetting something?!
- I remember...

01:34:11.350 --> 01:34:13.440
Jeez...

01:34:15.770 --> 01:34:18.200
I wonder if there still a way for us
to make the campsite...

01:34:19.610 --> 01:34:20.900
We'll think of something.

01:34:22.400 --> 01:34:25.200
Well, then, let's get going.

01:34:25.570 --> 01:34:26.660
Okay!

01:34:58.400 --> 01:35:00.610
Is anyone here...?

01:35:06.610 --> 01:35:08.410
It's completely empty.

01:35:08.490 --> 01:35:10.620
Did we get here too early?

01:35:15.580 --> 01:35:17.040
A pincecone!

01:35:17.100 --> 01:35:18.810
Hi there!

01:35:25.220 --> 01:35:27.010
Aki?

01:35:28.390 --> 01:35:29.800
What are ya doin'?

01:35:29.890 --> 01:35:31.600
There's some weirdos in there!

01:35:35.140 --> 01:35:37.520
Oh it's just Nadeshiko and Rin!

01:35:37.890 --> 01:35:41.520
It's just you guys! You scared me!

01:35:41.610 --> 01:35:43.340
But we didn't scare you off...

01:35:47.110 --> 01:35:50.280
I've been... waiting for you all.

01:35:59.000 --> 01:36:01.460
Hey there everyone!

01:36:01.540 --> 01:36:02.540
Hm?

01:36:03.500 --> 01:36:06.210
Oh my bad. I might've overdone it.

01:36:09.300 --> 01:36:13.220
So, we're all together once again!

01:36:13.310 --> 01:36:14.430
Yes!

01:36:14.810 --> 01:36:16.060
All right ladies!

01:36:16.140 --> 01:36:19.690
Currently, the prospects for the campsite
are pretty grim.

01:36:19.770 --> 01:36:22.560
So we need to change the situation...

01:36:23.020 --> 01:36:26.440
Inuko and I have been thinking about
how to approach this

01:36:26.520 --> 01:36:29.570
from both the prefectural side
and the archaeological side!

01:36:31.310 --> 01:36:34.510
1. Reconsider the plan

01:36:32.120 --> 01:36:34.450
First up we need to revise our plan!

01:36:34.950 --> 01:36:36.620
We need to revise it?

01:36:36.700 --> 01:36:40.580
So, well, the prefecture's new plan is to
make a ruins-related museum there.

01:36:41.250 --> 01:36:43.840
So instead of fighting it

01:36:43.920 --> 01:36:46.960
we'll propose a new campsite that
works with it.

01:36:48.170 --> 01:36:49.420
In short...

01:36:54.720 --> 01:36:57.600
You're really dedicated to this,
huh, Ogaki?

01:36:59.270 --> 01:37:01.100
Yes, completely!

01:37:02.670 --> 01:37:05.420
2. Speed up the excavation!

01:37:03.190 --> 01:37:05.360
Next, we need to speed up the excavation.

01:37:05.730 --> 01:37:10.110
The fact is that we're way behind schedule

01:37:10.650 --> 01:37:14.120
and we can't get back on track
until the dig is all done.

01:37:14.200 --> 01:37:18.080
So we're going to help them out.

01:37:20.210 --> 01:37:22.120
We'll be helping you starting today!

01:37:22.620 --> 01:37:24.460
Nice to meet you!

01:37:24.540 --> 01:37:26.380
You'll be a huge help!

01:37:26.800 --> 01:37:30.380
Oh yeah, after our shift,
I can even make lunch!

01:37:30.670 --> 01:37:31.720
Huh?

01:38:24.560 --> 01:38:27.980
Thank you for the food.
It really hit the spot.

01:38:28.060 --> 01:38:29.730
No, thank you!

01:38:29.820 --> 01:38:31.940
- Uh, I have a question...
- Hm?

01:38:32.280 --> 01:38:35.450
If you'd be down to teach me

01:38:35.530 --> 01:38:37.320
I'd love to learn about Jomon earthenware.

01:38:37.870 --> 01:38:39.030
Eh?

01:38:40.950 --> 01:38:42.830
You want to resume the series
about the campsite?

01:38:43.250 --> 01:38:47.330
Yes sir. The site is still a
work in progress

01:38:47.420 --> 01:38:48.840
but we're all trying our best.

01:38:49.420 --> 01:38:52.960
Of course I'll do this alongside
my currently assigned work

01:38:55.760 --> 01:38:59.220
- Go ahead.
-qu... Quickly.

01:38:59.890 --> 01:39:02.600
"Be sweet when you can be sweet."

01:39:03.640 --> 01:39:07.730
When I was younger my editor in chief
used to hound me all the time.

01:39:08.560 --> 01:39:10.860
You had a harsher upbringing than I.

01:39:10.940 --> 01:39:13.280
Eh, really?

01:39:14.740 --> 01:39:16.450
Thank you so much sir, Mr. Kariya.

01:39:22.240 --> 01:39:23.500
Next up we have

01:39:23.580 --> 01:39:27.710
an update on the excavation in Fujikawa.

01:39:28.120 --> 01:39:32.500
The current plan is to make a
small museum to display the findings...

01:39:32.590 --> 01:39:37.220
Excuse me but the Tourism Promotion Organization has a new proposal.

01:39:37.300 --> 01:39:38.470
Yes!

01:39:38.550 --> 01:39:41.140
Now, please take a look at this.

01:39:55.320 --> 01:39:57.530
For the last year we have been working

01:39:57.610 --> 01:40:01.030
on a facility established some time ago
in the Takaori area.

01:40:01.120 --> 01:40:04.200
During that time we have been making
a campsite.

01:40:05.370 --> 01:40:08.790
The original concept was "Reclamation."

01:40:09.330 --> 01:40:13.170
We were trying to make a place
where people can

01:40:13.250 --> 01:40:16.800
find enjoyment and new meaning
in what was already there.

01:40:17.970 --> 01:40:22.550
But when Jomon pottery was found
campsite development stopped.

01:40:22.890 --> 01:40:28.060
Yet even from this hiccup
we discovered and learned.

01:40:28.480 --> 01:40:30.810
These holes are called "mending holes."

01:40:31.230 --> 01:40:32.560
We believe that the holes

01:40:32.650 --> 01:40:36.570
were so a rope could be used
to hold together this cracked area.

01:40:36.940 --> 01:40:39.610
The people who lived back then wanted
to repair what was broken,

01:40:39.700 --> 01:40:42.530
it was a culture that care a lot
for the tools they used.

01:40:42.620 --> 01:40:43.830
Wow!

01:40:44.160 --> 01:40:45.410
Huh...

01:40:46.660 --> 01:40:50.080
When you camp you're far away
from your daily routine.

01:40:50.170 --> 01:40:52.630
It's a place where you can turn inward.

01:40:53.420 --> 01:40:56.630
We were trying to revitalize
this place

01:40:56.710 --> 01:40:59.050
but the campsite inspired us

01:40:59.130 --> 01:41:02.800
to reconnect with
old friends and ourselves.

01:41:02.890 --> 01:41:05.100
We could see what we had in front of us.

01:41:05.810 --> 01:41:09.680
From the Jomon pottery to the
old facility

01:41:09.770 --> 01:41:13.860
we can find insight into our lives today
from so many things around us.

01:41:13.940 --> 01:41:15.020
That's why...

01:41:16.780 --> 01:41:20.650
Our campground will keep the past alive!

01:41:20.850 --> 01:41:22.300
Camping and pottery!

01:41:26.920 --> 01:41:29.430
Archaelogical exhibition

01:41:29.430 --> 01:41:32.690
Historical activities

01:41:32.690 --> 01:41:36.190
Pottery firing bonfire

01:41:36.190 --> 01:41:41.080
Camping and history come together
in our new campsite proposal!

01:41:44.050 --> 01:41:47.310
And that is our new proposal
for the Takaori site.

01:41:47.680 --> 01:41:50.640
Thank you for your consideration!

01:42:02.280 --> 01:42:03.700
Alright.

01:42:04.910 --> 01:42:09.910
We will weigh it thoroughly against
any other proposals.

01:42:10.410 --> 01:42:11.410
Yes sir.

01:42:17.880 --> 01:42:19.840
Alright, let's get going!

01:42:19.920 --> 01:42:21.300
I'll be right there.

01:42:30.220 --> 01:42:31.430
Ogaki,

01:42:31.810 --> 01:42:34.310
This application form... huh?

01:42:34.730 --> 01:42:36.860
She's gone back to the room to prepare

01:42:37.190 --> 01:42:39.360
She said she wanted to tell
everyone the news.

01:42:56.620 --> 01:42:57.670
Okay.

01:43:01.400 --> 01:43:04.110
We're approved!

01:43:12.680 --> 01:43:16.600
Everything's grown in
the blink of an eye.

01:43:17.020 --> 01:43:19.860
You have real guts, growing again, grass.

01:43:20.150 --> 01:43:22.610
We have as much gumption as that grass!

01:43:23.070 --> 01:43:28.490
It won't be easy doing work in the Summer,
but we'll hit that Fall deadline somehow!

01:43:31.580 --> 01:43:34.750
Uhh... what's up?

01:43:34.830 --> 01:43:37.920
You're so motivational, Rin!

01:43:38.000 --> 01:43:39.540
Not really...

01:43:39.630 --> 01:43:42.000
Now a word from our leader!

01:43:42.090 --> 01:43:43.500
Eh?!

01:43:46.670 --> 01:43:47.720
Ahem.

01:43:48.430 --> 01:43:49.510
Fight!

01:43:57.230 --> 01:44:00.610
Let's start from the top and go
step by step.

01:44:00.690 --> 01:44:02.770
- Okay!
- Sounds good!

01:44:05.610 --> 01:44:08.280
This space here should be
for campers' tents.

01:44:08.860 --> 01:44:11.910
I'd like to make it as big as possible.

01:44:16.660 --> 01:44:18.790
- Alright.
- Okay!

01:44:19.170 --> 01:44:20.540
One, two...

01:44:24.710 --> 01:44:27.170
Whoops!

01:44:27.260 --> 01:44:30.800
Hahaha. You really need to
put your back into it!

01:44:31.090 --> 01:44:32.600
Mr. Okazaki!

01:44:35.640 --> 01:44:37.310
Take this!

01:44:45.480 --> 01:44:46.820
Just like that.

01:44:48.860 --> 01:44:52.240
Rin! Nadeshiko!

01:44:52.700 --> 01:44:54.240
Could you lend a hand?

01:45:01.670 --> 01:45:05.840
We've been given permission to take
whatever is left back here.

01:45:06.840 --> 01:45:09.720
It would be nice if we could use
this stuff for the kids' area.

01:45:29.280 --> 01:45:30.490
How is it?

01:45:32.450 --> 01:45:34.490
A-OK!

01:45:42.420 --> 01:45:44.960
It's really comin' down!

01:46:25.420 --> 01:46:27.790
Akari gave me this for the campsite.

01:46:33.300 --> 01:46:35.550
Have you guys invited your parents?

01:46:35.640 --> 01:46:36.680
Yeah.

01:46:36.760 --> 01:46:39.560
They're way more excited than I expected.

01:46:39.970 --> 01:46:43.180
I even invited the local shop owner!

01:46:43.270 --> 01:46:44.810
Akari is coming, too, right?

01:46:45.190 --> 01:46:46.730
She's coming in along with Ms. Toba and the others.

01:46:46.810 --> 01:46:49.480
She's coming in along with Ms. Toba and the others.

01:46:50.230 --> 01:46:51.940
Up we go.

01:46:52.400 --> 01:46:54.860
Maybe a little to the right?

01:46:54.950 --> 01:46:57.070
- Like this?
- Yeah.

01:46:57.160 --> 01:46:58.530
Alright！

01:47:34.490 --> 01:47:35.610
On three...

01:47:36.280 --> 01:47:38.740
We did it!!

01:47:46.330 --> 01:47:50.130
Let's see...
Consomee, salt and garlic.

01:47:50.540 --> 01:47:52.500
Do we need any olive oil?

01:47:52.590 --> 01:47:53.960
Ah, we do.

01:47:54.920 --> 01:47:57.380
It's been so long since I've gone camping.

01:47:57.970 --> 01:47:59.640
Alright, I'm off.

01:47:59.720 --> 01:48:02.390
- Be safe, okay?
- Okay.

01:48:12.900 --> 01:48:15.150
Your engine light came on, huh?

01:48:15.530 --> 01:48:18.400
You probably shouldn't drive until you can
take it in, just in case.

01:48:18.820 --> 01:48:21.410
How am I going to get to Takaori?

01:48:21.820 --> 01:48:24.200
Well... there might be a way...

01:48:36.880 --> 01:48:40.430
The reception form is printed and ready.

01:48:40.760 --> 01:48:43.180
We have change at the ready.

01:48:43.260 --> 01:48:45.140
The toilet's are all clean!

01:48:45.220 --> 01:48:46.680
Oh thanks!

01:48:47.020 --> 01:48:51.190
We have about 10 groups and
2 individuals coming today.

01:48:51.480 --> 01:48:52.810
Quite a few, huh?

01:48:52.900 --> 01:48:55.860
Half of them are acquaintances though.

01:48:55.940 --> 01:48:58.440
Not bad for a first day, I say!

01:49:01.070 --> 01:49:02.370
It's almost time!

01:49:02.450 --> 01:49:03.450
It is.

01:49:13.210 --> 01:49:14.290
Huh？

01:49:18.210 --> 01:49:19.760
Nobody's here...

01:49:21.430 --> 01:49:24.100
We haven't received any cancellations.

01:49:24.180 --> 01:49:28.310
Well it makes sense they might not
show up right on time.

01:49:28.390 --> 01:49:29.390
That tracks.

01:49:32.400 --> 01:49:35.520
You've reached the
Fujikawa Pinecone campsite.

01:49:37.020 --> 01:49:38.990
Wait, you don't know where we are?

01:49:40.240 --> 01:49:44.990
Keep an eye out for signs and
landmarks and we'll get back to you soon.

01:49:46.780 --> 01:49:49.500
I thought we had signs ready.

01:49:49.870 --> 01:49:52.580
- I mean, we all made them together.
- Yeah.

01:49:52.670 --> 01:49:54.250
- Hey guys...
- Hm?

01:49:54.670 --> 01:49:56.000
Are these them?

01:49:57.670 --> 01:49:59.760
What's the point of these if they're
not out there?

01:49:59.840 --> 01:50:03.470
This must be why our visitors haven't
arrived yet.

01:50:08.470 --> 01:50:10.890
Akari, can you tell where you are?

01:50:10.980 --> 01:50:14.310
I'm not really sure...

01:50:14.400 --> 01:50:16.810
I'm super lost!

01:50:16.900 --> 01:50:18.400
I'll go find them.

01:50:19.110 --> 01:50:23.610
Nadeshiko and Ena will direct me
to our lost visitors.

01:50:23.700 --> 01:50:24.780
- Yeah!
- Roger!

01:50:26.280 --> 01:50:29.160
The map in the brochure will make
it easier for them to get here, I think.

01:50:29.700 --> 01:50:31.750
They can see a shrine nearby!

01:50:32.330 --> 01:50:34.500
If there's a shrine in this area, it would be here.

01:50:34.580 --> 01:50:37.920
They might stand out because they're in a
white car with Yokohama plates!

01:50:38.000 --> 01:50:39.670
We're in your hands, Rin.

01:50:40.090 --> 01:50:41.420
Got it!

01:50:47.300 --> 01:50:48.390
I'm off!

01:50:48.450 --> 01:50:49.490
Leave it to me!

01:52:25.570 --> 01:52:27.240
So lively!

01:52:29.950 --> 01:52:34.790
These are the remains of a Jomon-era
living space that was found in a dig.

01:52:38.830 --> 01:52:41.170
It's about as big as a big tent!

01:53:04.980 --> 01:53:07.820
Did you invite the children from your
new school?

01:53:07.900 --> 01:53:12.070
Yes, I invited everyone!
They've become such fast friends.

01:53:14.830 --> 01:53:18.410
Nadeshiko, if you could...

01:53:18.500 --> 01:53:20.580
I'll be right over!

01:53:22.960 --> 01:53:25.500
As to be expected from a pro.

01:53:25.590 --> 01:53:27.590
Hah, maybe I am.

01:53:27.670 --> 01:53:31.340
Oh... hey Rin!

01:53:39.430 --> 01:53:40.480
Rin.

01:53:44.810 --> 01:53:46.230
Grandpa.

01:53:47.190 --> 01:53:50.280
You came, welcome.

01:53:50.360 --> 01:53:51.360
I did.

01:53:52.700 --> 01:53:55.620
- I see you've finished it.
- Yeah.

01:54:03.250 --> 01:54:04.630
It's a good campsite.

01:54:08.500 --> 01:54:09.630
Thank you.

01:55:14.280 --> 01:55:16.110
Everyone looks so happy.

01:55:16.200 --> 01:55:17.200
They do.

01:55:18.030 --> 01:55:21.700
- I'm so happy!
- Yeah.

01:55:22.950 --> 01:55:24.710
I'm glad we did it.

01:55:24.810 --> 01:55:25.940
Yeah.

01:55:26.390 --> 01:55:27.710
Yeah.

01:55:28.210 --> 01:55:29.210
Yeah.

01:55:29.710 --> 01:55:30.710
Yeah.

01:55:31.210 --> 01:55:32.210
Yeah.

01:55:36.430 --> 01:55:40.100
How about we come here for this
New Year's Eve?

01:55:40.180 --> 01:55:41.600
Oh good idea!

01:55:41.680 --> 01:55:45.520
We could see a Diamond Fuji for our
first sunrise of the year.

01:55:45.600 --> 01:55:46.890
What would we eat?

01:55:46.980 --> 01:55:49.610
It's New Years, so why don't we
have soba?

01:55:50.150 --> 01:55:51.860
And you'll be there too, Rin, right?

01:55:55.650 --> 01:55:56.860
Maybe.

01:56:02.740 --> 01:56:03.870
For now...

01:56:05.660 --> 01:56:07.120
I'll think about it.

01:56:31.580 --> 01:56:34.960
Fujikawa Revitalization Project

01:56:31.580 --> 01:56:34.960
-Campsite management and operation

01:56:31.580 --> 01:56:34.960
- Region revitilization

01:57:06.740 --> 01:57:10.410
Sobaudon

01:57:32.100 --> 01:57:34.100
Want to go camping with your pet?

01:57:52.370 --> 01:57:55.630
"How Far Can My Moped Take Me"
Project Proposal
